    "title": "Emmy Noether: Modern LaTeX Working Corpus and Multilingual Translation Drafts (R823 Source Control and Synchronized Components)",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21419257",
    "publication_date": "2026-07-17",
    "description": "<p>This is the reader-facing Emmy Noether working record for the Modern LaTeX Editions of Mathematics Manuscripts project. This version fronts <code>00_Noether_German_Cumulative_Working_SourceControl_v26_R823_20260717.pdf</code>, a 466-page German working reader. Its editable TeX, direct source witnesses, before/after renders, audit records, and build transcripts are grouped in file <code>07</code>.</p><p><strong>German R823 change:</strong> Paper 20 printed pages 27-31 were reopened directly against the GDZ article witness. R823 restores the source run-in quotient and binomial-count prose, removes a non-source display gap, restores two em-dash parentheticals, and restores equation (14) punctuation. No OCR text was promoted.</p><p><strong>New synchronized components:</strong> file <code>09_Noether_R823_SourceSynchronized_Multilingual_Components_20260717.zip</code> contains source-synchronized standalone English components for Papers 10, 20, 26, 28, 29, and 37; bounded R823-controlled Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Japanese, and Korean outputs for Papers 26 and 36; and the R823 lecture-book title/introduction in Ukrainian, Russian, Interslavic Latin, and Interslavic Cyrillic. Each component carries its own source, build, terminology, visual-QA, and checksum evidence where available.</p><p><strong>Open work:</strong> the retained full English reader is the older RA10 working branch; the full Chinese and Japanese readers have not been rebased unit by unit to R823; Korean coverage is currently limited to bounded notices; and the Slavic book-front component is 1 of 32 core book units. The previously published Paper 06 Slavic tranche remains a working translation requiring fresh line-by-line reconciliation.</p><p><strong>Status caveat:</strong> this is a serious source-repair and translation working corpus, not a critical edition, author-wide or paper-by-paper source-faithfulness certification, synchronized multilingual corpus, native-language approval, or publication-grade proofreading. Local task words such as <code>COMPLETE</code>, <code>closed</code>, or <code>ready</code> refer only to bounded components.</p><p><strong>GitHub:</strong> corrections, source comparisons, LaTeX fixes, and translation improvements can be suggested via issues or pull requests at <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
